      overviewBody:
        'Debuting in 1994 with five compulsory subjects graded 0–15, GSAT replaced the joint entrance exam\u2019s one-shot verdict. The Star Program and personal application — together over half of all university seats — both start from GSAT. The 2018 curriculum reform retired the five-subject total grade and opened free subject choice (departments count up to 4); AY111 split math into A/B, formalizing six freely elective subjects. Officially, the change was meant to let “specialists” find their fit. In practice, 56,021 AY115 examinees (46.09%, a record three years running) took all six subjects — a rational strategy to keep every option open.',
